[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090] 
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   Step 090 -- bias-free mean-plane warp of the distant Kuiper belt
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   (Siraj, Chyba & Tremaine 2025 estimator) and the direction of the warp
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   Siraj, Chyba & Tremaine (2025, MNRAS Letters slaf091; arXiv:2508.14156)
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   introduced a likelihood mean-plane estimator that is, by construction,
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   independent of the survey footprint: conditioning on each object's
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   observed position r-hat removes the on-sky selection function w(r)
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   from the likelihood, leaving only the intrinsic orbital-plane term.
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   They report a warp of the distant Kuiper-belt mean plane relative to
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   the invariable plane in the 80-200 AU (2.5 sigma) and 80-400 AU
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   (2.7 sigma) semimajor-axis bins -- i0 ~ 15 deg toward node Omega0 ~
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   120 deg -- and show in their own n-body tests that NEITHER the
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   Brown-Batygin (2021) Planet Nine NOR their own Siraj+25 Planet-X
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   realization can generate it; a third, distinct perturber ('Planet Y',
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   ~0.06-1 M_earth, a = 100-200 AU, i >~ 10 deg) would be required.
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   This step (i) re-implements the exact estimator on real MPCORB
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   elements -- an orbit-fit lineage independent of JPL SBDB -- (ii)
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   reproduces the warp in their semimajor-axis bins on two samples
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   (their published 46-object Table-1 list, and a pipeline-native
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   non-resonant cut), and (iii) asks the question their paper leaves
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   open: WHERE does the disk lean?  The mean-pole offset azimuth is
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   measured against the detached-TNO boundary axis (lam=49 deg) already
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   recovered by the resident and transit channels, and against the
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   published perturber planes.
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   Likelihood (their eq. 16)
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   log L = gamma * m_hat . sum_i J_hat_i
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   - sum_i log I0( gamma * sin(theta_i) ) + const
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   with m_hat the trial mean-plane pole, J_hat_i = r_i x v_i / |r_i x v_i|
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   the angular-momentum direction, and theta_i the angle between m_hat
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   and the observed position r_hat_i.  Delta log L is profiled over
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   gamma at the invariable plane (i_inv = 1.6 deg, Om_inv = 107 deg);
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   significance = sqrt(2 Delta log L) (their convention).  The false-
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   alarm probability is measured by Monte-Carlo: synthetic disks
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   distributed symmetrically about the invariable plane, drawn at the
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   OBSERVED position vectors (the von-Mises-on-the-tangent-circle
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   generative null of SCT25, conditioned on the real on-sky geometry so
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   the C_i denominators match the data exactly).
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   Positions are propagated from MPCORB osculating elements
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   (a, e, i, Om, w, M at the file epoch, K2669 = 2026-06-09 for >99 per
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   cent of rows) by two-body Kepler solution -- heliocentric ecliptic;
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   the heliocentric-vs-barycentric offset is far below the estimator's
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   resolution and is recorded as a caveat.
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   Non-resonant cut: objects within +/-1.5 per cent in semimajor axis of
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   a Neptune mean-motion resonance (p+q):p with p+q <= 12 are excluded --
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   an analytic proxy for the SBDynT 90-clone filter used by SCT25, run
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   at +/-1.0 and +/-2.0 per cent as sensitivity checks.
[2026-09-20 12:04:10 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 090]   Outputs
